 "description": "Tone+FX 3.2a by Digital Alchemy DSP (github.com/DigiAlchemydsp/RingTone), ported from its original FM-groovebox version: a master effect suite on every output: main, headphones and USB. Master ring modulator, a low-shelf/high-shelf master EQ (TILT), a Crunch/Redux lo-fi stage (BITS / SR / CRUNCH), a wavefolder with a continuous CLEAN/MUD/DIST/TRSH fold type, a five-mode modulation insert (PITCH: WOB / SHFT, STEREO: FLAN / PAN / WIDE), an output meter and a soft output ceiling. Seven pages after the stock master pages (FUNC+LFO; LEFT/RIGHT rotate the pages): DIGI RING, FOLD, TILT, CRUSH, PITCH, STEREO and PERFORM. PERFORM is reached with UP from any of the six: the eight knobs set one depth per FX block, and the 16 trigs are momentary performance pads (four blocks of four intensities: ring / fold+crush / pitch / pan) that ramp their block up while held and back on release. Settings follow the pattern while the unit is on (they are not saved over a power cycle on the DT1), and the FX answer incoming MIDI CC. From 3.2a4 its pages and its master stage are core 4.1's (master pages, ev_render_master), so it combines with Digi EQ. The unit starts with its own intro (no boot splash).",
